---
/**
 * Your First Cast-On (E-wrap) - Skill Builder Page
 * Slug: /practice/skill-builders/your-first-cast-on/
 * 
 * This is a starter template with placeholders. 
 * Replace content marked with TODO comments.
 */
import SkillBuilderLayout from "../../../../components/skill-builders/SkillBuilderLayout.astro";

// =============================================
// FAQ DATA - Single source of truth
// Edit here to update both visible FAQ and JSON-LD schema
// =============================================
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "My yarn keeps falling off the needles during cast-on",
    answer: "Make sure each wrap is snug but not too tight. The yarn should sit securely in the needle hook. Try wrapping slightly further back on the needle. Use the fingers of your opposite hand or a transfer tool to guide the loops."
  },
  {
    question: "The first row is too tight and hard to knit",
    answer: "This is common! Try loosening your tension dial by 1–2 numbers for just the first row, then adjust back to your normal setting."
  },
  {
    question: "I'm getting dropped stitches on the edges",
    answer: "Check that your end needles are properly wrapped. Edge stitches often need a slightly firmer wrap. Also ensure your weights are evenly distributed."
  },
  {
    question: "The carriage won't move smoothly after cast-on",
    answer: "Your cast-on may be too tight. Gently tug down on the cast-on comb to give the needles room to move. If it persists, you may need to restart with a looser wrap. Try wrapping every other needle. Knit 1 row and put all needles in work and continue to knit"
  },
  {
    question: "How do I know if I'm wrapping in the right direction?",
    answer: "For E-wrap, wrap counter-clockwise around each needle when viewed from above. The yarn should form an \"e\" shape. Consistent direction matters more than which direction you choose."
  }
];
---

<SkillBuilderLayout
  title="Your Start & Finish"
  subtitle="Cast On & Bind Off"
  price="$19"
  level="Beginner"
   metaDescription="A clear demonstration of one cast on and one bind off, showing how the edge forms at the start and finish of your knitting."
  faqs={faqs}
>

  <!-- ======================= -->
  <!-- B) QUICK SCAN SECTION   -->
  <!-- ======================= -->
  <div slot="quick-scan">
    
    <!-- TODO: Replace placeholder content below -->
    <div class="sb-scan-card">
      <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-user-check"></i> Best For</h3>
      <!-- TODO: Replace with actual "Best For" content -->
      <p>New machine knitters seeing a cast on and bind off for the first time, and knitters who want a quick refresher.</p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="sb-scan-card">
      <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-list-check"></i> You'll Need</h3>
      <!-- TODO: Replace with actual "You'll Need" content -->
      <ul>
        <li>Your knitting machine (any brand)</li>
        <li>Yarn appropriate for your machine (light color, medium weight recommended)</li>
        <li>Claw weight, Cast-on comb (optional)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="sb-scan-card">
      <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> Watch For</h3>
      <!-- TODO: Replace with actual "Watch For" content -->
      <ul>
        <li>Tension too tight on first row</li>
        <li>Missing needles during wrap</li>
        <li>Yarn not seated in latches</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
  </div>

  <!-- ======================= -->
  <!-- C) WHAT YOU'LL DO       -->
  <!-- ======================= -->
  <div slot="what-youll-do">
    <!-- TODO: Replace placeholder paragraph -->
    <p>You’ll cast on, knit a short practice piece, and bind off to see how the edge forms at the start and finish. By the end of this Skill Builder, you’ll have completed a sample swatch and know what to expect from these techniques when you begin a project.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- ======================= -->
  <!-- D) VIDEO SECTION        -->
  <!-- ======================= -->
  <div slot="video">
    <div class="kbm-video-grid">
      <!-- LEFT COLUMN: Text/context -->
      <div class="kbm-video-text">
        <h3 class="kbm-video-heading">Watch first</h3>
        <ul class="kbm-video-tips">
          <li>This video demonstrates the complete E-wrap cast-on from start to finish</li>
          <li>Pay attention to how the yarn wraps around each needle</li>
          <li>Notice the tension and hand positioning</li>
        </ul>
        <button type="button" class="kbm-modal-trigger" id="optionalVideoTrigger" aria-haspopup="dialog">
           <i class="fa-solid fa-play"></i> Optional Video: Open vs Closed — what edge did you just make? (5 min)
        </button>
      </div>
      
      <!-- RIGHT COLUMN: Main video thumbnail -->
      <div class="kbm-video-embed">
        <button type="button" class="kbm-video-thumbnail" id="mainVideoTrigger" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="Play E-Wrap Cast On video">
          <img src="https://vumbnail.com/151860058.jpg" alt="E-Wrap Cast On video thumbnail" loading="lazy" />
          <span class="kbm-play-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 68 48" width="68" height="48">
              <path d="M66.52 7.74c-.78-2.93-2.49-5.41-5.42-6.19C55.79.13 34 0 34 0S12.21.13 6.9 1.55c-2.93.78-4.63 3.26-5.42 6.19C.06 13.05 0 24 0 24s.06 10.95 1.48 16.26c.78 2.93 2.49 5.41 5.42 6.19C12.21 47.87 34 48 34 48s21.79-.13 27.1-1.55c2.93-.78 4.64-3.26 5.42-6.19C67.94 34.95 68 24 68 24s-.06-10.95-1.48-16.26z" fill="#212121" fill-opacity="0.8"/>
              <path d="M45 24L27 14v20" fill="#fff"/>
            </svg>
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <!-- BIND OFF VIDEO GRID -->
    <div class="kbm-video-grid" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <!-- LEFT COLUMN: Text/context -->
      <div class="kbm-video-text">
        <h3 class="kbm-video-heading">Finish your swatch</h3>
        <ul class="kbm-video-tips">
          <li>This video demonstrates a stitch-through-stitch bind off worked by hand</li>
          <li>Notice how stitch size affects the finished edge</li>
          <li>Watch how the yarn is controlled as stitches are worked off the machine</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      
      <!-- RIGHT COLUMN: Bind off video thumbnail -->
      <div class="kbm-video-embed">
        <button type="button" class="kbm-video-thumbnail" id="bindOffVideoTrigger" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="Play Stitch-Through-Stitch Bind Off video">
          <img src="https://vumbnail.com/252258022.jpg" alt="Stitch-through-stitch bind off video thumbnail" loading="lazy" />
          <span class="kbm-play-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 68 48" width="68" height="48">
              <path d="M66.52 7.74c-.78-2.93-2.49-5.41-5.42-6.19C55.79.13 34 0 34 0S12.21.13 6.9 1.55c-2.93.78-4.63 3.26-5.42 6.19C.06 13.05 0 24 0 24s.06 10.95 1.48 16.26c.78 2.93 2.49 5.41 5.42 6.19C12.21 47.87 34 48 34 48s21.79-.13 27.1-1.55c2.93-.78 4.64-3.26 5.42-6.19C67.94 34.95 68 24 68 24s-.06-10.95-1.48-16.26z" fill="#212121" fill-opacity="0.8"/>
              <path d="M45 24L27 14v20" fill="#fff"/>
            </svg>
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ======================= -->
  <!-- E) STEPS SECTION        -->
  <!-- ======================= -->
  <div slot="steps">
    <!-- Printable checklist link -->
    <div class="kbm-print-link">
      <a href="/downloads/skill-builders/your-first-cast-on-practice-checklist.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Download the practice checklist (PDF)
      </a>
      <span class="kbm-print-helper">Print this for your machine-side notes.</span>
    </div>
    
    <ol class="sb-steps">
      <li>
        <!-- TODO: Replace step 1 -->
        Set up your machine on a stable surface and thread your yarn through the tension mast.
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- TODO: Replace step 2 -->
        Bring out the needles you want to use to the working position (usually 20–40 needles for practice).
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- TODO: Replace step 3 -->
        Starting from the left, wrap the yarn around each needle in an E-wrap pattern.
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- TODO: Replace step 4 -->
        Hang your cast-on comb and weights on the wrapped stitches.
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- TODO: Replace step 5 -->
        Set your tension dial to the recommended setting and slowly push the carriage across.
      </li>
      <li>
        Knit 10–20 rows to create your practice swatch.
      </li>
      <li>
        Prepare to bind off by pulling all needles forward and removing the yarn from the carriage.
      </li>
      <li>
        Work the stitch-through-stitch bind off by hand, keeping the stitches even as you remove them from the needles.
      </li>
      <li>
        Secure the final stitch and leave a short tail.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <!-- ======================= -->
  <!-- F) PRACTICE SECTION     -->
  <!-- ======================= -->
  <div slot="practice">
    <!-- TODO: Replace placeholder practice bullets -->
    <ul class="sb-practice-list">
      <li>Try casting on 20 needles, then 40 needles to feel the difference</li>
      <li>Experiment with different tension settings (note which feels best)</li>
      <li>Practice the E-wrap motion until it feels natural</li>
      <li>Time yourself: aim to cast on 40 stitches in under 2 minutes</li>
      <li>As you bind off, adjust stitch size slightly and notice how it changes the feel of the edge</li>
    </ul>
    
    <!-- Practice Swatch Callout -->
    <div class="sb-practice-callout">
      <!-- TODO: Replace placeholder practice swatch content -->
      <strong>Practice Swatch:</strong> Aim to create a small swatch (about 4" x 4") using your new cast-on skills. Keep this swatch! It's proof of your progress and helpful for comparing tension later.
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- G) TROUBLESHOOTING - Now auto-generated from faqs prop above -->
  <!-- No slot needed - edit the faqs array in the frontmatter -->

  <!-- ======================= -->
  <!-- H) TERMS USED           -->
  <!-- ======================= -->
  <div slot="terms-used">
    <dl class="sb-terms-list">
      
      <!-- TODO: Replace/update term definitions -->
      <div class="sb-term">
        <dt>Open Cast-On</dt>
        <dd>A cast-on method that creates an open, loopy edge. The bottom of your knitting isn't closed, allowing you to pick up stitches later or unravel from the bottom.</dd>
      </div>
      
      <div class="sb-term">
        <dt>Closed Cast-On</dt>
        <dd>A cast-on method that creates a finished, sealed edge. The bottom is closed and neat—you won't be able to unravel from this end.</dd>
      </div>
      
      <div class="sb-term">
        <dt>Stitch-Through-Stitch Bind Off</dt>
        <dd>A hand-worked bind off where each stitch is pulled through the next to form a chained edge with adjustable stretch.</dd>
      </div>
      
    </dl>
  </div>

  <!-- ======================= -->
  <!-- I) WHAT'S NEXT          -->
  <!-- ======================= -->
  <div slot="whats-next">
    <!-- TODO: Replace placeholder links with actual URLs -->
    <div class="sb-next-buttons">
      <a href="#" class="sb-next-btn">
        <!-- TODO: Replace with actual next skill builder link -->
